{
  "date": "2026-11-19",
  "category": "finance",
  "title_zh": "证监会：“基金公司要上报AI投资数据”的说法不是真的",
  "title_en": "CSRC: The claim that fund companies must report their AI investment data is not true",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "zh": "11月18日，中国证监会新闻发言人回答了记者的问题。最近网上有一条消息说，监管部门要求基金公司上报所有产品在AI方面的投资情况。发言人表示，这条消息不是真的。",
      "en": "On November 18, a spokesperson for the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) answered reporters' questions. Recently, a message online said that regulators had asked fund companies to report the AI-related investments of all their products. The spokesperson said this message is not true."
    },
    {
      "zh": "公募基金是面向普通大众销售的基金。发言人说，公募基金买哪些股票和债券、每种买多少，都由基金公司按照基金合同自己决定。证监会也没有要求基金公司提交这方面的数据。",
      "en": "Public mutual funds are funds sold to the general public. The spokesperson said that which stocks and bonds a public fund buys, and how much of each, is decided by the fund company itself according to the fund contract. The CSRC has also not asked fund companies to submit data of this kind."
    },
    {
      "zh": "同一天，资本市场辟谣平台也发布消息，说网上一个关于国务院常务会议的说法是谣言。这个说法称，会上有人表示以后不会再经常“救市”。这个平台11月8日开始运行，由中国上市公司协会负责运营。",
      "en": "On the same day, the capital market rumor-refuting platform also published a notice saying that a claim online about a State Council executive meeting was a rumor. The claim said that someone at the meeting stated the government would no longer often \"rescue the market\". The platform started running on November 8 and is operated by the China Association for Public Companies."
    },
    {
      "zh": "今年证监会已经处罚了一些在网上传播假消息的人。比如在4月，一名微博账号的运营者被罚款80万元，而且3年内不能进入证券市场。",
      "en": "This year the CSRC has already punished several people who spread false information online. For example, in April the operator of a Weibo account was fined 800,000 yuan and banned from the securities market for 3 years."
    }
  ],
